        "Execution plan snapshots and attempt history are durable",
        "Logical steps materialize unfrozen (PENDING, frozenSpecHash/frozenAt null) and freeze only when a claim or gate decision becomes authoritative; engine-level reconcileExecution is the single idempotent autonomous progression path and resumeAfterResult is a compatibility alias",
        "Targeted dispatchAttempt(stepAttemptId) gives claim-to-dispatch affinity; dispatchNext/recover() is the global background drain with per-record retryable isolation and a bounded batch; terminal dispatch failures are reconciled against the execution that actually owns the attempt",
        "Legacy migration backfills StepAttempts only from persisted evidence (COMPLETED->SUCCESS, FAILED->FAILED, CANCELLED->CANCELLED, RUNNING->RUNNING); never-attempted/ambiguous rows stay attempt-free and no invalid status is ever written; overwritten legacy retry history is documented as non-reconstructable",
        "Real-PostgreSQL integration coverage (concurrency, affinity, fairness, legacy-schema adoption) runs only when TEST_DATABASE_URL is provided",
        "AgentEvent/watchdog persistence remains outside Milestone 0"
      ]
